.TH PARSE_EDAC_TRACE 1 "2024-01-15" "arm-linux-fault-resilience" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
parse_edac_trace \- parse kernel EDAC / AER / MCE log traces into structured JSON
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B parse_edac_trace.py
[\fB\-i\fR \fIFILE\fR]
[\fB\-o\fR \fIFILE\fR]
[\fB\-\-event\-types\fR \fITYPES\fR]
[\fB\-\-pretty\fR]
[\fB\-\-stats\fR | \fB\-\-no\-stats\fR]
[\fB\-\-log\-level\fR \fILEVEL\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B parse_edac_trace.py
reads a Linux kernel ring buffer log (dmesg output, journald export, or a
captured log file) and extracts hardware error events from the EDAC, PCIe
AER, and Machine Check Event (MCE) subsystems into a structured JSON format.
.PP
The output JSON is suitable for postmortem analysis, replay via
.BR replay_kernel_state.sh (1),
and ingestion into Prometheus via the node_exporter textfile collector.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-i ", " \-\-input " " \fIFILE\fR
Input log file. Use
.B \-
for stdin (default).
.TP
.BR \-o ", " \-\-output " " \fIFILE\fR
Output JSON file. Use
.B \-
for stdout (default).
.TP
.B \-\-event\-types \fITYPES\fR
Comma-separated list of event types to include.
Valid values: \fBCE\fR, \fBUE\fR, \fBAER_CE\fR, \fBAER_UE\fR, \fBMCE\fR.
Default: all types.
.TP
.B \-\-pretty
Pretty-print JSON output with 2-space indentation.
.TP
.B \-\-stats
Print parse statistics to stderr after parsing (default: enabled).
.TP
.B \-\-no\-stats
Suppress statistics output.
.TP
.B \-\-log\-level \fILEVEL\fR
Set the logging level. One of \fBDEBUG\fR, \fBINFO\fR, \fBWARNING\fR, \fBERROR\fR.
Default: WARNING.
.SH OUTPUT FORMAT
Each event is a JSON object with the following fields:
.TP
.B seq
Integer event sequence number (0-based).
.TP
.B event_type
One of: CE, UE, AER_CE, AER_UE, MCE.
.TP
.B subsystem
One of: EDAC, AER, MCE.
.TP
.B controller
Memory controller identifier, e.g. "MC0".
.TP
.B count
Number of errors represented by this event.
.TP
.B timestamp_str
Original timestamp string from the log.
.SH SUPPORTED LOG FORMATS
Raw dmesg, journald \fB\-o short\-monotonic\fR, syslog with timestamps, and
stripped logs without timestamps are all supported.
.SH EXAMPLES
Parse a captured kernel log and write pretty-printed JSON:
.PP
.nf
.RS
python3 replay/parse_edac_trace.py \\
    \-\-input /var/log/kern.log \\
    \-\-output errors.json \\
    \-\-pretty
.RE
.fi
.PP
Filter for correctable errors only, pipe to jq:
.PP
.nf
.RS
python3 replay/parse_edac_trace.py \-\-event\-types CE | jq '.[] | .controller'
.RE
.fi
.PP
Generate a synthetic log and parse it:
.PP
.nf
.RS
python3 tools/generate_edac_log.py \-\-events 100 \\
    | python3 replay/parse_edac_trace.py \-\-pretty
.RE
.fi
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Success.
.TP
.B 1
Input file not found or unreadable.
.TP
.B 2
Parse error or invalid arguments.
